id: hac-djof
title: Implement typed frontend version and semantic resource commands
description: "Add a typed ws frontend command family for version, themes, icons, and translations with strict category/input validation, deterministic flattening, count/filter/limit bounds, complete help, capability probes, docs, and tests."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[6]: agents,frontend,implementation,localization,typescript,websocket
created_at: "2026-08-07T05:48:29.648Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T06:05:17.302Z"
deadline: "2026-08-08T05:48:29.648Z"
assignee: codex-root
claim_principal: codex-root
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "A focused source module under 300 LOC registers version, themes, icons, and translations; categories and CSV integration inputs validate before connection; resource-heavy responses support count and positive limit bounds with deterministic ordering; capability metadata, focused tests, E2E help, docs, and exact coverage are updated; live read-only commands succeed without persisting private output"
definition_of_ready: Official current Core schemas and live compatibility are proven; feature hac-fj2b and approved plan hac-pzfs exist; all-status duplicate search found no frontend semantic catalog item.
goal: best-agent-home-assistant-cli
objective: implement-typed-frontend-semantic-catalog
value: Safe discoverable semantic metadata for agent planning and presentation.
impact: Eliminates raw protocol construction and unbounded localized payloads for common frontend discovery.
outcome: Four typed read-only commands with exact automated and live proof.
why_now: Current Home Assistant localization and icon contracts are the supported source after action translation removal from get_services.
parent: hac-pzfs
reviewer: unbraind
risk: medium
confidence: 98
sprint: frontend-intelligence
release: 2026.8.7
